### Delete a platform that has no publication rows
# Prereqs:
# - Azurite running and the Azure Functions host started.
# - The `local` environment is selected and `accessToken` is set in
#   `http-client.env.json.user`.
#
# Scenario 1: a platform that was never published to. Create a throwaway
# platform with PlatformCrud.http, copy its id here, and delete it.
# Expected response: 204 No Content. The platform disappears from
# GET /api/platforms and leaves no orphan history because it had no
# Published rows.

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/platforms/REPLACE_WITH_UNPUBLISHED_PLATFORM_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Confirm the deleted platform is gone
# Expected response: 404 Not Found for the same id.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/platforms/REPLACE_WITH_UNPUBLISHED_PLATFORM_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete a platform that has a Published publication row (orphan history)
# Scenario 2: a platform that was published to. Set this up first:
#   1. Create a YouTube platform (PlatformCrud.http) with OAuth values minted
#      for the target channel (see docs/api/operations/youtube-publish-setup.md).
#   2. Create a future calendar event with an English title
#      (CalendarEvents/CreateCalendarEvent.http).
#   3. Publish the event to the platform (CalendarEvents/EventPlatforms.http)
#      so its publication row becomes Published.
#   4. Delete the platform here.
# Expected response: 204 No Content. The platform is removed, but its Published
# publication row is preserved as read-only orphan history. Verify with the
# event platform listing request below: the item still appears with
# `platformDeletedUtc` set and `canPublish: false`.

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/platforms/REPLACE_WITH_PUBLISHED_PLATFORM_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Confirm the published row survives as orphan history
# Replace the calendar event id with the one you published in step 2-3 above.
# Expected response: 200 OK. The deleted platform still appears in `items` with
# `status: "Published"`, `platformDeletedUtc` set, and `canPublish: false`.

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/calendar-events/REPLACE_WITH_CALENDAR_EVENT_ID/platforms
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete an unknown platform
# Expected response: 404 Not Found.

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/platforms/00000000000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete a platform with a publish in progress (conflict)
# A platform delete is rejected with 409 Conflict while any of its publication
# rows is `Publishing`. The Publishing state is transient (it exists only during
# an in-flight publish), so it is hard to hold open with manual requests. This
# request documents the expected contract; reproduce it only if you can pause a
# publish mid-flight. Expected response under that condition: 409 Conflict.

DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/platforms/REPLACE_WITH_PUBLISHING_PLATFORM_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
